---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Trust & Safety — ArmorClaw" description="How ArmorClaw keeps your data safe and your agent accountable.">
  <section class="px-6 py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="mb-8 text-4xl font-bold text-white">Trust &amp; Safety</h1>
      <p class="mb-12 text-lg text-[#8b8b92]">
        ArmorClaw is built around a simple principle: you own your data,
        you control what the agent can do, and you can verify both at any time.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-10">
        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Your data stays local</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-[#8b8b92]">
            All memories, chats, workspaces, and commitments live in a SQLite
            database on your machine at
            <code class="rounded bg-[#26262c] px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-[#d97706]">~/Library/Application Support/ArmorClaw/</code>.
            ArmorClaw never uploads your data to our servers. The only network
            calls are to your chosen model provider (OpenAI or Anthropic) using
            your own API key, and to our license server for subscription validation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Secrets in Keychain</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-[#8b8b92]">
            API keys and OAuth tokens are stored in macOS Keychain, protected by
            your system password. They never appear in plaintext in config files,
            logs, or the database.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Irreversible actions require approval</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-[#8b8b92]">
            Every action the agent takes is classified as reversible or irreversible.
            Irreversible actions (sending emails, deleting data, making purchases)
            always require your explicit approval, regardless of your autonomy settings.
            The <code class="rounded bg-[#26262c] px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-[#d97706]">gated</code> default
            means even reversible actions wait for approval until you opt in to autonomous mode.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Full audit trail</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-[#8b8b92]">
            Every significant action is logged in the audit log: workspace and
            project creation/deletion, memory approvals and rejections,
            commitment executions, and more. You can review the full log in
            Settings &rarr; Audit Log at any time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Workspace export</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-[#8b8b92]">
            Export your entire workspace as structured markdown files at any time.
            Your data is never locked in. If you cancel, you keep everything.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Cancel anytime</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-[#8b8b92]">
            One click in Settings &rarr; Account to cancel your subscription.
            You receive a prorated refund for the remaining days. No retention
            dark patterns, no "are you sure" loops.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
